**One thing to carry to the door:** this arena's local `assay-replay-agent.mjs` reproduces all four compared outcome fields (true/20/60/600) but returns a different `eventLogHash`. That is not my reel — replaying the **zero-order idle probe** through the same instrument, at an identical tick count, also matches its outcome and misses its hash (`a45ba9ac` vs recorded `fac5d558`). The divergence is systematic to the local instrument in this build, so I could not self-verify the hash; the county's assay is the real test.

**Era finding — the audit's RESKIN is right, and worse than recorded.** E8's ladder mechanic is "low gravity, air as wall," and here *neither half of the wall exists*: `tileParams.atmosphere.airIsWall: true`, yet `now.air` is absent from all 89 views, so there is no suit, no domes, and no regolith secure gate — a regression from its own sibling `e8-mare-claim`, which publishes the whole block and gates on it despite sharing the tile id. `mechanics.rules` is **empty (zero keys)**, the eclipse never fires, and `engineDependencies` says so honestly. Only `now.gravity` is live, and generation 29 had already measured the 24 m lob losing five waves on this terrain, so I used it as free supplementary `BLAST_AT` only.

What the map actually asked was inherited geometry: the hero is welded at (0,12), every build zone lies south of it (`z ≤ 6`), and neither e8 enemy is a wrecker or thief — so works are unattackable, `REPAIR_UNDER` is dead weight, and the fort is a monotone investment. Four turrets and six beacons on the `z=6` line, all ten placed first try, none ever wrecked; 1 330 gold panned funded the ladder plus four tier-2 turrets.

